  "problem_statement": "The UNICoAP options unit tests need a macro `UNICOAP_OPTIONS_ALLOC_STATIC(name, capacity)` that creates a statically allocated UNICoAP options object for use with the existing UNICoAP options API. In the tests it is called as `UNICOAP_OPTIONS_ALLOC_STATIC(options, 100)` and `UNICOAP_OPTIONS_ALLOC_STATIC(options, 900)`. The macro must make `options` available as an options container with a storage buffer of the requested capacity, and it must be usable immediately by the existing option manipulation functions without requiring a separate initialization step.",
